Upgrade Node.js from 20.18.2 (Buildroot 2024.02 default) to 24.21.0.

Three things beyond the version bump:

1. c-ares, libuv and nghttp2 are switched from the system copies to the ones
   bundled in the Node tree. Buildroot 2024.02.x carries c-ares 1.27.0,
   libuv 1.48.0 and nghttp2 1.64.0, while Node 24.21.0 bundles and validates
   against newer releases (nghttp2 1.70.0). Only the bundled combination is
   tested upstream, so link those statically instead of relying on the older
   system libraries. zlib and OpenSSL stay shared - Node 24 has no hard
   minimum for OpenSSL and Buildroot's 3.2.4 satisfies the >= 3.2 feature
   checks in src/crypto/crypto_util.h.

2. 0001-add-qemu-wrapper-support.patch is dropped and the wrapper is wired in
   through Node's own mechanism instead.

   That patch injected an @MAYBE_WRAPPER@ marker in front of every build tool
   gyp has to execute, then sed'd it to the qemu wrapper path. Node 24 does
   this natively: node.gyp and tools/v8_gypfiles/v8.gyp carry '<@(emulator)'
   slots in front of node_js2c, node_mksnapshot, torque, mksnapshot,
   bytecode_builtins_list_generator and gen-regexp-special-case, defaulting to
   an empty list via "'emulator%': []," in common.gypi. The old patch no
   longer applies against those files (2 of 4 hunks in node.gyp and 1 of 5 in
   v8.gyp are rejected), and there is no reason to carry it: NODEJS_SRC_WRAPPER_FIXUP
   now points the native slots at the wrapper. The host build needs no fixup
   at all, since the empty default expands to nothing - so
   HOST_NODEJS_SRC_WRAPPER_FIXUP is gone too.

   Note configure.py's --emulator option is NOT usable here: it is silently
   ignored whenever --cross-compiling is passed, which Buildroot always does.

3. The linux-armv7l hash is dropped. Node stopped publishing official 32-bit
   ARM builds, so there is no such tarball for 24.x.

Hashes are from https://nodejs.org/dist/v24.21.0/SHASUMS256.txt
The LICENSE hash is calculated locally from node-v24.21.0.tar.xz.

diff --git a/package/nodejs/nodejs-src/0001-add-qemu-wrapper-support.patch b/package/nodejs/nodejs-src/0001-add-qemu-wrapper-support.patch
